{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then layer specifications that map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe recovery/exploration action. Forward motion is the default in clear conditions, random_walk is used only as a mild coverage bias after successful forward progress, obstacle states force short directed turns, and a rare front-obstacle branch allows one brief backward escape before turning. A dedicated stuck helper enables full_rotate only after repeated front-blocked outcomes.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability using plant automata.",
    "Encode policy with small deterministic specifications: clear->move_forward, post-forward clear->random_walk, left obstacle->rotate_clockwise, right obstacle->rotate_counterclockwise, front obstacle->brief backward then directed turn, repeated front blockage->last-resort full_rotate."
  ],
